<speak>I am glad the setting has been comfortable. A planned call gives both sides a chance to have the necessary notes ready and reduces the temptation to rush between unrelated subjects. For future meetings, we can retain that approach without making the arrangements overly formal. You can bring a short list of administrative questions if you have them, and we can keep a separate note of anything that belongs with a specialist support team. That way the relationship conversation does not become a technical troubleshooting session halfway through. Different kinds of assistance can still be coordinated without having to happen all at once.</speak>